{"scenario":"dts-arq-reset-never-acked-link-lost","rows":["C-0255","C-0257","C-0739","C-0791","C-0804","C-0866","C-1170","C-1172","C-1173","C-1250","C-1251","B-0276","B-0277","B-0324","K-0074","A-0321"],"source":"Ed4 C.4.7.3, pp.C-37 to C-39; C.7.4, pp.C-108 to C-109; C.7.5.2.1, p.C-112","description":"A FULL RESET CMD that the peer never acknowledges is repeated at each dts.reset_wait expiry until the sixteenth unanswered wait, when the DTS declares the connection lost and the link is broken locally.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","csma":{"mode":"jitter"},"modem":{"preamble_ms":600,"flush_ms":150,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":25,"block_ms":4800}]},"cas":{"max_links":4,"link_request_timeout_ms":60000,"link_request_retries":2,"first_data_timeout_ms":120000},"dts":{"ack_wait_ms":60000},"sis":{"soft_link_idle_ms":3600000,"soft_link_min_hold_ms":3600000,"soft_link_max_ms":3600000}},"note":"Conn 1 binds SAP 9 for ARQ at 0. As dts-arq/sync-test-1-fail-full-reset up to 156550: the link is made at 57550, the peer\u0027s FSN 0 and 1 are delivered at 61000 and acknowledged at 83000, and at 96000 the peer\u0027s DATA-ONLY with FSN 0 fails Test 1, so this node starts a FULL RESET (C-0791, C-1170): FULL RESET CMD, RESET FRAME ID 0 (C-1173), out at 151000; dts.reset_wait/0.0.1.3 starts at 156550 with dts.ack_wait_ms, 60000 (C-1172). Here no FULL RESET ACK ever comes. At each expiry the same command, same RESET FRAME ID, goes again (C-0255, C-1172): LBT 3000 after our own transmission (K-0074), then contention, then the 15-byte, one-block transmission (5550 ms), then dts.reset_wait again. Each expiry is an answer wait that ended with no answer from the peer (C-1250); the peer sends nothing meanwhile. The sixteenth in a row is not followed by a repeat: the DTS declares the connection lost (C-0739, C-1250): D_CONNECTION_LOST to the CAS, then the connection ends with nothing to reject (C-1251, C-0866), and the CAS breaks the link locally (B-0277, B-0324): link_state unlinked and C_PHYSICAL_LINK_BROKEN to the SIS. cas.first_data stopped at 61000 and no other timer runs. Fixture: preamble 600, flush 150, 25 bytes and 4800 ms a block, so an n-block transmission lasts 750 \u002B 4800 n ms, and the EOT of a D_PDU starting in block b of n is ceil((4800 (n - b) \u002B 150) / 500): 10, 20, 30 for 1, 2, 3 blocks to go (C-0104, C-1043). Addresses 0.0.1.2 (this node) and 0.0.1.3 take address size 3 (C-0133). A CAS-1 C_PDU of one octet in a type 8 D_PDU fills a block exactly (25 bytes; EOT and reception window 10), C_PDU IDs from 0 in each node\u0027s own sequence (C-1040), EOW 0. RESET/WIN-RESYNC (type 12) 15 bytes; DATA-ONLY 19 bytes plus segment; ACK-ONLY 15. Seed 0 draws uniform(16) = 15, 4, 15, 12, 11, 10, 1, 12, 3, 6, 9, 6, 11, 15, 9, 11, 5, 6: contention waits 45000, 12000, 45000, 36000, 33000, 30000, 3000, 36000, 9000, 18000, 27000, 18000, 33000, 45000, 27000, 33000, 15000, 18000 ms (K-0080). The soft link times are set to 3600000 so that no SIS close falls within the run; the SIS starts sis.soft_link_min_hold (called node only), sis.soft_link_max and sis.soft_link_idle when the link is made, and stops the idle wait while an ARQ U_PDU is outstanding (A-0320, A-0321, A-0326)."}
